.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH "bead show" 1  "bead show " 
.SH NAME
bead show \- Show a single issue
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBbead show\fR [\fB\-\-json\fR] [\fB\-\-comments\fR] [\fB\-\-fields\fR] [\fB\-\-notes\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fIID\fR> 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Display detailed information about a single issue.
.PP
Shows complete issue details including dependencies, labels, and optionally
comments. JSON output is one issue object.
.PP
EXAMPLES:
  bead show bead\-123abc456789def                    # Human\-readable output
  bead show ID \-\-json                                # One issue object as JSON
  bead show ID \-\-comments unresolved                 # With unresolved comments
  bead show ID \-\-comments all \-\-json                 # Full issue with all comments
.PP
OUTPUT FORMAT:
  Without \-\-json: Human\-readable detailed view
  With \-\-json: One JSON object for the issue
.PP
COMMENT PROJECTION:
  \-\-comments none         Show only counts and resolution metadata (default)
  \-\-comments unresolved   Include bodies for unresolved comments only
  \-\-comments all          Include all comment bodies in canonical order
.PP
FIELD PROJECTION:
  \-\-fields a,b,c          Emit only the named cli_issue document members (per
                          record for list) in text, \-\-json, and \-\-jsonl
                          output. Unknown names exit 2 naming the valid set;
                          the set is published by the field guide:
                            bead schema explain urn:bead\-rs:schema:issue:native\-v1
                          Without \-\-fields every member is emitted.
.PP
NOTES PROJECTION:
  Appended history belongs in comments (R010), not notes: JSON consumers
  re\-read notes in full, so keep notes bounded context.
  \-\-notes auto            Default. \-\-json/\-\-jsonl keep the full notes member
                          (unchanged NEEDLE contract); text views print the
                          last 2000 characters preceded by an omission line
  \-\-notes none            Omit the notes member entirely
  \-\-notes tail:N          Last N characters of notes
  \-\-notes all             The full notes member
.PP
ISSUE DETAILS INCLUDE:
  \- Basic fields: id, title, description, priority, status
  \- Assignment: assignee (if any)
  \- Manual block: manual_blocked flag (true when explicitly blocked)
  \- Effective status: effective_status (shows \*(Aqblocked\*(Aq when manual_blocked is true)
  \- Timestamps: created_at, updated_at, closed_at (if closed)
  \- Dependencies: blocked_by (blocking issues), blocking (issues this blocks)
  \- Labels: all assigned labels
  \- Comments: based on \-\-comments projection
  \- Metadata: issue_type, close_reason (if closed)
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR
Output in JSON format
.TP
\fB\-\-comments\fR \fI<COMMENTS>\fR [default: none]
Comment projection: none, unresolved, or all (default: none)
.TP
\fB\-\-fields\fR \fI<FIELDS>\fR
Comma\-separated projection of cli_issue document members (FIELD PROJECTION); without it every member is emitted
.TP
\fB\-\-notes\fR \fI<MODE>\fR [default: auto]
Notes projection: auto, none, tail:N, or all (default: auto)
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.TP
<\fIID\fR>
Issue ID
